@nsobid-4B159F0F7A360669738390EE8657B4F0

# ASTRAL CHAIN 1.0.1 - Disable SMAA

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables the post-process anti-aliasing pass. Astral Chain has no FXAA filter
// at all; its post AA is SMAA, run as the three FilterSMAAEdge / FilterSMAAWeight
// / FilterSMAABlend passes at the very end of the frame.
//
// One flag decides whether they run. It is the AND of three conditions: the AA
// quality setting allows it, the game is docked, and the renderer's SMAA feature
// bit is set. When it is true the tone-mapped image is redirected into a
// scratch target and the SMAA chain blends it onto the real one; when it is
// false the image goes straight to the real target and the chain is skipped.
// Handheld mode already takes that second path every frame, so forcing the flag
// to zero produces the engine's own no-AA output rather than a new code path.
//
// This patches the frame code, not a config default, so an option screen or a
// settings file cannot turn it back on.

@enabled
00402AE0 19008052   // MOVZ W25,#0 (was AND W25,W9,W8,LSR#26 = the SMAA enable flag)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against ASTRAL CHAIN 1.0.1 (PlatinumGames "Hw"
// framework, PRJ_036, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was
// located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
